			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847140">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights</strong>: Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: The most average man in the world, who's everything (height, weight, general routine, you name it) is very normal, has the unconscious power to remove the abnormal properties of every anomaly he comes across temporarily, if not erase it completely, provided that they should remain under his observable range or presence. Doesn't realize his powers, since every anomalous event is forcibly made to look normal to him.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>: The Normality was found by accident when one of the SCP broke containment and coincidentally ran into him, henceforth being neutralized and re-secured. At first the foundation takes an interest in him, trying to recruit him since he could be a key to neutralizing all anomaly.</p>
<p>However, none of the foundation members were able to approach him due to his nature, and they decided instead to use him indirectly, by testing and putting forward SCPs to be erased. However, when they planned on erasing a keter class using him, it results in the foundation almost collapsing, since the foundation itself could be considered an anomaly, and anything that could affect his normal life gets influenced by his ability.</p>
<p>After closely preventing that, further testing and attempts to erase anomalies was stopped, because every anomaly he encounters afterwards carries the risk of letting the foundation come under his influence. Hence he was given SCP status, put under watch, and was prevented from coming in contact with anything abnormal.</p>
<p><strong>Hooks</strong>: SCP is famous for trying to keep the most anomalous in check. It would interest both new and old fans to see how they would try to deal with the opposite. Also, the foundation's primary goal is to preserve reality and order. The normality could show an outlook on when moving towards that very goal can be disastrous.</p>
<p><strong>Additional notes</strong>: This is my first SCP. Please tell me how may I improve on this, if any.</p>

