															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/i-remain-yours-truly" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7100953); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7100953&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609834223" alt="i_remain_yours_truly" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7100953)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/i-remain-yours-truly" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7100953); return false;" >i_remain_yours_truly</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608288715 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Dec 2020 10:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847638">
									

<p>Hi.<br />
I've read your crit and I wanted to clear some things.<br />
Firstly, I wasn't aware of the Djoric-Dmatix Proposal and its similarity to my idea until now. Thank you for that.<br />
Secondly, while your concern about them being similar are true, I think they are different in essence:<br />
1.) The Djoric-Dmatix Proposal, or the thirty-six, are somewhat aware of what they are capable of, and are part of something huge. However, the normality is just an average person, who lives an average life not knowing what he is and what he could do, and with no part of something grandiose.</p>
<p>2.) The normality does not influence anomalies over a large area, just that which is under his observation or could potentially affect his normal life. This shows that if he was left alone, he would not have affected the foundation or anything at all, and even now, with proper precaution, could be controlled, unlike the thirty-six</p>
<p>3.) The Thirty-Six are contained because they possess a risk of generating large amounts of anomaly upon death, and affecting the entire world. The normality is observed for a different reason, that is, his power to bring equilibrium could wipe out the foundation's existence without actually ending the world, not for threatening reality as we now know it. In other words, the normality is given SCP status not because he is anomalous, but rather because he is normal, a bit too much.</p>
<p>I am sure that you will have more concerns. If so, please do not hesitate to give me your feedback<br />
Thank you</p>

